WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:05.910
The Minister for Balanced Regional Development, Milan Krkobabić, has for a long time

2
00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:10.570
been warning about the dismal demographic statistics in villages in southern Serbia,

3
00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:14.710
where more than 1200 rural communities are on the verge of disappearing.

4
00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:19.490
Of course, the state has neither the resources nor the ability to save every one,

5
00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:25.030
but the National Village Rescue Team has identified a hundred that have a chance to survive

6
00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:28.990
and that could become a locomotive of development for at least 3–4 neighboring settlements.

7
00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:33.230
The outlines of a large-scale campaign that will bring these villages back to life,

8
00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:36.910
the minister announced 3 months ago at the Cooperative Congress in Niš.

9
00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:45.230
We deal with questions of existence, to be precise: agriculture united in cooperatives,

10
00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:54.850
family businesses, rural tourism, various kinds of ethnotourism, hunting, resort tourism,

11
00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:57.090
and then infrastructure problems —

12
00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:06.630
not so much regional and local roads as access roads, field roads, water supply,

13
00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:12.790
I mean above all digging wells for technical and drinking water,

14
00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:16.450
and then we deal with problems of the social standard,

15
00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:21.210
that is, the construction or commissioning of multifunctional facilities,

16
00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:29.930
where we'd have both a post office and a clinic, and a multifunctional hall for cultural events,

17
00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:33.970
and meeting places for the oldest and meeting places for the youngest,

18
00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:37.690
and work on certain sports facilities.

19
00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:45.150
The fourth segment concerns the protection of heritage, cultural and natural, in these parts of Serbia.

20
00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:51.050
In the city of Pirot, which itself has long been struggling with dismal statistics in the villages on Stara Planina,

21
00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.730
the announcement of this three-year project brings great relief,

22
00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:58.390
because they themselves barely cope with the many accumulated problems.

23
00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:03.690
The villages that are near the city, let's say, on our ring road,

24
00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:09.290
are quite lively, full of young people engaged in agriculture,

25
00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:19.770
full of able-bodied people, and the farmland in this lowland part is mostly cultivated.

26
00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:25.450
But if you go a bit uphill, toward Stara Planina or from the other side toward Vlaška Planina,

27
00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:30.570
the situation is completely different. Very few residents live in these villages.

28
00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:35.490
They are, of course, inclined to do only farming.

29
00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:42.590
Some of them are pensioners, but even in retirement they engage in some small-scale farming.

30
00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:50.570
That is, it's not commercial production, so the picture is completely different from what's seen in the Pirot valley.

31
00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:57.470
Stara Planina abounds in boundless pastures and watercourses, so it's ideal for extensive livestock raising,

32
00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:01.790
but right now on this mountain beauty there are neither people nor sheep.

33
00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:08.070
I've been in this business for more than 30 years, and when I began working,

34
00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:11.710
there were about a hundred thousand sheep in the Pirot district.

35
00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:15.150
In the city of Pirot there were more than 60 thousand sheep.

36
00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:20.230
Today in Pirot, on the territory of the city, we have only about 10 thousand sheep.

37
00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:24.070
Sheep were bred mainly on Stara Planina.

38
00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:26.870
Now there are very few sheep on Stara Planina,

39
00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:30.590
they have come down to the villages near the city,

40
00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:34.990
because it's easier for herders to get their produce to market,

41
00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:38.350
get to the market and sell their produce,

42
00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:42.250
which in the end is everyone's goal — to earn something from this produce.

43
00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:46.350
At the Ministry of Agriculture they talk a lot about developing livestock raising too,

44
00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:51.910
but the big problem is the lack of people and motivation among people,

45
00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:55.870
because it's obvious that in the village there are no more young people, at least in our part,

46
00:03:55.950 --> 00:04:01.710
who would launch some more serious livestock or agricultural production.

47
00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:06.450
Our interviewee welcomes the idea of the Ministry for Balanced Regional Development

48
00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:10.450
to also help entrepreneurs who would open mini-workshops in villages,

49
00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:14.990
because that would perhaps be the best lure for young people to return to their native villages.

50
00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:22.930
The information now coming from the Ministry for Balanced Regional Development —

51
00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:28.650
that funds will be allocated to both farms and entrepreneurs — is very good news,

52
00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:31.990
and, I think, it should have happened much earlier.

53
00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:37.730
The state itself should have, through some regulations, exempted all investors who invest

54
00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:44.850
in these depopulated areas for ten years or even more

55
00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:49.850
from paying certain state fees, exempted from certain taxes

56
00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:54.910
the jobs that would be opened there, because even in these mountain villages

57
00:04:54.910 --> 00:05:02.030
you can open production in line with the local resources that are there.

58
00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:05.910
Small sawmills could have been opened, small fish farms made,

59
00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:13.670
cooperatives created that would buy potatoes, process medicinal herbs, etc.

60
00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:19.090
The opportunities were, are, and exist today too, but it's necessary to distinguish

61
00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:24.170
from an investor who invests in the vicinity of Belgrade.

62
00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:28.770
Today it's completely the same whether you build a plant in Požarevac, in Belgrade

63
00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:30.690
or build it on Stara Planina.

64
00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:35.390
However, our field research showed that even entrepreneurs,

65
00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:38.550
who have a great desire to invest in villages, hesitate —

66
00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:44.290
precisely because of the lack of workforce and the infrastructure needed to build a workshop.

67
00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:49.390
So, for example, the former director of Pirot's "Tigar" decided to produce craft beer

68
00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:52.530
and sells it exclusively in his native village of Dojkinci.

69
00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:58.670
Although this drink would be much tastier if it were made with mountain village water,

70
00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:01.350
the workshop was nevertheless built in Pirot.

71
00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:06.070
It's our strategic goal, but, unfortunately, we haven't achieved it yet.

72
00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:10.070
It's just that the main problem there is labor.

73
00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:15.430
You know, the village is quite old, like all villages in Serbia.

74
00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:22.450
Old people live there, and people from Pirot hardly decide to go there to work and stay overnight.

75
00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:29.670
Especially young people. It's a real paradox. People without jobs, but they just don't want to go outside Pirot.

76
00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:36.110
So for us that's the main problem, especially with the technologist who would have to be kept there, in the village.

77
00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:43.430
But overall it would really be exceptionally good — to make beer from that mountain water.

78
00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:50.970
The largest producer of "pressed sausage" in these parts doesn't plan to move production to any of the Stara Planina villages either.

79
00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:57.690
As for "pressed sausage," the livestock and raw materials have always come from Stara Planina,

80
00:06:57.690 --> 00:07:02.470
and the processing was in Pirot.

81
00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:10.550
They have huge pastures there, especially on Stara Planina.

82
00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:15.830
I think they should primarily breed livestock and focus on breeding, cattle raising,

83
00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.670
and processing, maybe, can be elsewhere.

84
00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:24.610
In principle, I'm sure everyone should do their own thing and that a division of labor is needed.

85
00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:29.650
A big chance for the revival of rural areas here is seen in the development of rural tourism.

86
00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:34.490
Perhaps the biggest, as yet unused potential belongs to the stone village of Gostuša,

87
00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:40.130
where the masonry of houses without binding mortar and with roofs of stone slabs has been preserved.

88
00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:44.330
The reconstruction project of this authentic old settlement

89
00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:49.430
received the "Europa Nostra" award and the European Union Grand Prix in 2016.

90
00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:54.590
This autumn the reconstruction of the local church began, several families started

91
00:07:54.610 --> 00:08:00.670
engaging in rural tourism, but the growing interest in Gostuša has also led to negative tendencies.

92
00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:05.210
Namely: more and more locals are restoring their great-grandfathers' hearths,

93
00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:08.450
but instead of stone slabs, roof tiles are turning red on the houses,

94
00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:15.250
which violates the architectural ensemble that the state also declared a protected cultural asset in 2018.

95
00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:19.270
When you do it with slabs, the investment is large.

96
00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:30.430
In one day he takes off the slabs, puts up rafters, and on the second day has already laid the tiles.

97
00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:33.090
And it will cost him, maybe, 100–200 thousand dinars.

98
00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:36.030
And if he did it with slabs, he'd have to pay 500 thousand dinars.

99
00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:44.890
And with their own money, of course; sometimes I say: why do you do it like this? And they say: with our own money we do what we want.

100
00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:58.870
For this to be possible, someone needs to come to our aid, give at least some funds.

101
00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:02.030
Let it not be 100%, not 50%, let it be 30%.

102
00:09:03.070 --> 00:09:08.690
It's precisely here that the state must react first of all, otherwise an exceptional tourist chance will be lost,

103
00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:12.470
says the director of the Pirot Tourism Organization, Bratislav Zlatkov.

104
00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:17.010
I know that a so-called passport has been made for every house,

105
00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:22.050
but what's lacking for the people who intend to take up tourism more seriously there,

106
00:09:22.190 --> 00:09:26.610
and for us too, is funds precisely for the reconstruction of these old houses,

107
00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:30.330
to put them in order and put them in the service of tourism development.

108
00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:35.690
I think as long as there are no sufficiently accessible loans, so to speak,

109
00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:38.890
or some subsidies, non-repayable in the end, as there once were,

110
00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:43.510
so that these people might take up the development of this part more actively.

111
00:09:43.630 --> 00:09:47.230
We will, of course, try: everything connected with the tourism organization,

112
00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:52.770
all the sights and places located above the village, below the village and by Zavoj Lake —

113
00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:55.270
to promote as much as possible and try to mark them,

114
00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:57.670
to create something new for guests.

115
00:09:57.670 --> 00:10:03.090
There are plans, but we need a bit more support from both the Institute and the state.

116
00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:08.910
And what tourist potential lies in preserving Gostuša is best shown by the example of neighboring Bulgaria,

117
00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:18.130
on the other side of Stara Planina, where in Gabrovo our neighbors opened the "Etar" museum of old crafts back in 1964,

118
00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:22.930
and just 19 kilometers from there tourists can also visit the stone village of Boženci,

119
00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:26.790
which in architecture is very similar to our Stara Planina villages.

120
00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:33.790
Rivers of tourists flow there every year, and Gabrovo and Boženci are also a must-visit place for school excursions.

121
00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:39.450
Perhaps with the help of European Union funds something similar could be done here too.

122
00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:45.890
However, even if this project is realized, the residents of Gostuša would still be far from the tourist dinar,

123
00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:50.830
because due to the lack of field roads it is hard for them to reach their fields and pastures.

124
00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:58.550
What torments us most is that the people who are returning now are mostly 65 years old, I tell you, they're still strong.

125
00:10:59.270 --> 00:11:05.270
Most of them would like to keep at least a cow, at least a sheep, at least some goat.

126
00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:14.230
There are no roads, we've already applied four or five times to our municipality of Pirot,

127
00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:19.010
applied for roads to be built to the barn, so that a person can get to his land.

128
00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:23.350
Since I pay tax, I should have access to this property.

129
00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:29.330
And yet, as for basic road infrastructure, the city of Pirot can boast excellent results,

130
00:11:29.510 --> 00:11:33.130
because even the most remote villages can be reached on asphalt.

131
00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:37.730
We have four or five villages whose access is difficult,

132
00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:44.890
but we're doing our best to make better roads to those villages too.

133
00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:49.710
Of course, paving the way to one village where 10 or 15 residents live,

134
00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:53.450
and which costs 50 or 60 million, puts you before a big dilemma:

135
00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:58.530
whether to invest these funds so they get an asphalt road,

136
00:11:58.930 --> 00:12:02.590
which, of course, they should have, but I must say, on the other hand,

137
00:12:02.690 --> 00:12:06.350
we have more than 300 kilometers of local roads that we maintain.

138
00:12:06.430 --> 00:12:11.250
With the changes to the Law on Roads we received some roads that used to be maintained by the state.

139
00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:16.570
Now these roads have also been handed over to us for maintenance, but we still allocate in the budget

140
00:12:16.570 --> 00:12:21.310
about 500 million for infrastructure works in the city and in the villages.

141
00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:27.030
So I can confidently say that up to 90 percent of our villages

142
00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:31.630
can be reached on asphalt, and only a very small number of deserted villages

143
00:12:31.630 --> 00:12:36.250
have no asphalt access.

144
00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:41.230
A few years ago the Babušnica Tourism Organization made an excellent

145
00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:45.270
move by organizing "Vurdijada" — a festival devoted to promoting

146
00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:51.750
the local dairy delicacy, which in two days in October attracts up to 20,000 guests here.

147
00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:57.730
Thanks to "Vurdijada" several farms and enterprises seriously took up this production.

148
00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:06.250
Over these seven years eight "Vurdijadas" have been held, we've reached roughly 40–50 participants in the vurda category,

149
00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:13.210
the festival itself has grown to 190 participants, the festival venue has changed, and the whole infrastructure,

150
00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:15.470
as the festival grew, so did we.

151
00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:19.430
"Vurdijada" created conditions for a dozen farms to live off vurda,

152
00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:24.290
for serious volumes to be produced and sold throughout the south of Serbia,

153
00:13:24.350 --> 00:13:28.030
and, of course, lately it's available in Belgrade too,

154
00:13:28.330 --> 00:13:32.490
but compared with the market's potential the production is much smaller,

155
00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:36.370
so this product still has room for growth.

156
00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:40.630
And in our municipality closest to the Bulgarian border, Dimitrovgrad,

157
00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:44.410
a festival has been held for some time now devoted to the local meat delicacy —

158
00:13:45.230 --> 00:13:49.870
the Caribrod šušenica, which has already become known among tourists from Serbia and Bulgaria.

159
00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:54.630
However, it shows that the Village Rescue Team will have to work a lot on the ground

160
00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:59.430
with the rural population to use the market chances that already exist.

161
00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:03.510
For now, at the šušenica festival, because of the inertness of cattle breeders,

162
00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:08.050
others skim the cream, the veterinarian and farmer Aleksandar Vasov told us,

163
00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:12.050
who in the village of Protopopinci raises sheep and goats and makes cheese.

164
00:14:12.690 --> 00:14:18.730
What I would reproach our farmers for now is a lack of enterprise.

165
00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:24.350
What's happening? The festival was invented, it's being held for the fifth time,

166
00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:29.830
there's buyer interest, and farmers see their benefit in selling their animals

167
00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:34.050
to some enterprising person who will process them further and take them away,

168
00:14:34.150 --> 00:14:35.750
skimming the cream, the added value.

169
00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:38.650
Instead of organizing themselves and presenting their own product.

170
00:14:38.970 --> 00:14:42.310
So this is a reproach to farmers, they're inert.

171
00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:46.530
A friend of mine complained to me, I asked: well, why did you sell the sheep?

172
00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:50.870
He says: all spring nobody came to me for lambs.

173
00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:54.090
And I tell him: buddy, nobody ever came to me, not in a single year.

174
00:14:54.450 --> 00:15:00.110
Offer. And it has to be so. Times change, and the farmer must change.

175
00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:05.290
What we see as a problem in these modern times may also be a big chance,

176
00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:10.370
because the world is increasingly turning to nature, healthy food and individual tourism,

177
00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:16.650
which offers the traveler authentic experiences, and the Balkans, which have kept their soul, offer exactly that.

178
00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:19.630
That's why the Serbian Village Revival Team has a lot of work ahead,

179
00:15:19.630 --> 00:15:25.170
but also the chance to give the rural communities of southern Serbia hope for a better tomorrow.